.TH JOTDO 1 2026-10-26 "jotdo 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jotdo \- reminders from your CalDAV server, in a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jotdo
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B jotdo
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A CalDAV server (Nextcloud, Radicale, Ba\(:ikal, Fastmail and most others)
keeps task lists alongside calendars, and Apple Reminders, Tasks.org and jtx
Board show them as reminder lists.
.B jotdo
reads and writes those lists directly, so a phone sees an edit made in jotdo
as an edit.
.PP
Without a command, jotdo opens a browser with the account's lists, Today,
Scheduled and an agenda of the coming days. A repeating reminder that is
ticked off moves to its next date. If a reminder changes on the server while
it is open, the save is refused and the text is kept.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list " [\fIlist\fR]"
Open reminders, by due date.
.TP
.B today
Reminders due today, and overdue ones.
.TP
.BR all " [\fIlist\fR]"
Open and finished reminders.
.TP
.BI show " reminder"
Print a reminder.
.TP
.BR new " [\fIfields\fR] [\fItitle\fR]"
Add a reminder; without a title, write it in
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.BI set " reminder fields"
Change only the fields given.
.TP
.BR edit " \fIreminder\fR [\fIfile\fR]"
Edit in
.BR $VISUAL " or " $EDITOR ,
or replace from
.IR file .
.TP
.BI done " reminder..."
Tick off.
.TP
.BI undone " reminder"
Tick back on.
.TP
.BI rm " reminder"
Delete.
.TP
.BR agenda " [\fIdays\fR]"
Events and reminders for the coming days.
.TP
.B lists
The account's lists and calendars.
.TP
.BR events " [\fIdays\fR]"
Calendar events for the coming days, numbered.
.TP
.BR "event new" " [\fIevent-fields\fR] \fItitle\fR"
.TQ
.BI "event show" " event"
.TQ
.BI "event set" " event event-fields"
.TQ
.BI "event rm" " event"
Add, print, change and delete calendar events. Deleting a repeating event
deletes the whole series.
.PP
.I reminder
is a number from
.BR list ,
.B today
or
.BR all ,
or the start of a reminder's UID.
.I event
is a number from
.B events
or the start of an event's UID.
.SH FIELDS
For
.B new
and
.BR set :
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title " \fItext\fR"
(set only)
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list " \fIname\fR"
Which list.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-due " \fIwhen\fR"
.BR "tomorrow 9am" ", " fri ", " "oct 24" ", " "2026-10-24 18:00" ", " "in 2h" ;
.B none
clears it.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-repeat " \fIrule\fR"
.BR daily ", " weekdays ", " "every 2 weeks" ", " "every mon, wed" ", " monthly ,
or an RRULE.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-alert " \fIwhen\fR"
.BR "at due" ", " "15m before" ", " "1h before" ;
several with commas.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-priority " \fIlevel\fR"
.BR high ", " medium ", " low ", " none .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-notes " \fItext\fR"
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-url " \fIurl\fR"
.PP
For
.B event new
and
.BR "event set" :
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-start " \fIwhen\fR"
As for
.BR \-\-due ;
a date alone makes an all-day event.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-end " \fIwhen\fR"
Read relative to the start.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-for " \fIlength\fR"
.BR 1h ", " 90m ", " "2 days" .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-calendar " \fIname\fR"
.TQ
.BR \-L ", " \-\-location " \fItext\fR"
.TQ
.BR \-n ", " \-\-notes " \fItext\fR"
.TQ
.BR \-A ", " \-\-alert " \fIwhen\fR"
.TQ
.BR \-r ", " \-\-repeat " \fIrule\fR"
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account " \fIname\fR"
An account from the configuration. The default is the configuration's
.BR default .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON instead of text, for every command but the browser.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR j " " k ", arrows"
Move.
.TP
.BR tab ", " h " " l
Switch between the lists and the reminders.
.TP
.BR space ", " x
Tick off, or back on.
.TP
.B a
Add: a title, and a due date after
.BR " @" .
.TP
.B n
New reminder in the editor.
.TP
.BR enter ", " e
Edit.
.TP
.B d d
Delete.
.TP
.B c
Show finished reminders.
.TP
.B /
Search;
.B esc
clears.
.TP
.B r
Reload.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/jotdo/config.toml
Accounts and settings, for example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
default = "home"
agenda_days = 7
clock = "12h"            # or "24h"

[accounts.home]
url = "https://cloud.example.com"
user = "me"
password_command = "pass show cloud/app-password"
default_list = "Personal"
# ca_file = "~/certs/my-ca.pem"
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B password_command
runs through
.BR /bin/sh ;
the first line of its output is the password.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/mmoyles87/jotdo
